@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Method / document navigation. Scope-independent process/navigation; provider or runner examples are not MVP prerequisites.
title Resumefolio | Requirements change and actual disposition
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
 BorderColor #64748B
 FontColor #17324D
 DiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
 DiamondBorderColor #B45309
 StartColor #17324D
 EndColor #17324D
}
start
:Record actual request, source, reason and affected revision;
:Classify editorial / proposed refinement / material commitment change;
:Assess proportional behavior, access, data, quality, cost and delivery impacts;
if (Material product / commitment / baseline decision required?) then (yes)
 :Present concrete options and reviewed proposal;
 if (Actual owner disposition authorizes this change?) then (yes)
  :Apply only the authorized scope and conditions;
 else (pending / rejected / deferred)
  :Retain actual outcome, rationale and obligations;
  :Do not imply acceptance or bypass retained gate; <<#FEF3C7>>
  stop
 endif
else (within existing authorized editing scope)
 :Proceed within existing request / authority;
endif
:Update affected primary records, definitions, scenarios and trace links;
:Identify changed revision and perform actual relevant recheck;
:Record evidence / open findings and preserve superseded history;
stop
legend bottom
Routine authorized document edits do not create product-policy acceptance.
No new planning DEC or baseline decision exists without an actual decision.
Historical inspected hashes remain attached to their original bytes.
endlegend
@enduml
